    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0677" n="639" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg639"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.1 House, Edward M.:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-02T15:00:00+01:00">September 2, 1919—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4002. Strictly confidential for the Secretary of State only [from Polk]. House
                    writes that President wishes him to return to Paris.<anchor n="92"
                        xml:id="d323-f1"/> Please send me a message to be decoded by me advising me
                    reason of his return and my position in the Mission as regards him. Will he be
                    head of delegation? Any arrangement will be satisfactory, but I would like to
                    know grounds for move. Polk.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
